// A project with real source and NO tests in it, so `maxon test` has somewhere honest to find
// nothing.
//
// It exists for the one assertion the rest of the fixture cannot make: a run that discovers zero
// tests exits 1, never 0. A harness that answers "0 tests, all green" is the CI lie this command
// was built to refuse — a renamed directory or a broken glob then reads as a passing suite for
// months, and nobody looks at a green light.
//
// It is a sibling of testsample/ rather than a directory inside it, because `maxon test` takes a
// PROJECT: a subdirectory of testsample/ would be part of testsample's own compile and would
// inherit its tests.

function main() returns ExitCode
	print("this project has source but no tests\n")

	return 0
end 'main'
